HakiOS port of the OnePlus 8T (KB2000, SM8250 "kona") — NOTICE

This repository is a device port for HakiOS:
  HakiOS — https://github.com/oosexgang/hakios-xnu-kernel (MIT, and APSL-2.0 for its XNU work)
The kernel patch here is that project's work rebased onto xnu-10002.1.13 (iOS 17.0.0):
  XNU — https://github.com/apple-oss-distributions/xnu (Apple Public Source License 2.0)
  Theos — https://github.com/theos/theos and https://github.com/theos/sdks (MIT and Apple's SDK terms)
  Mu-Silicium — https://github.com/Project-Silicium/Mu-Silicium (the UEFI HakiOS starts from; not
  distributed here: uefi/apply.sh fetches it)

What is not here, on purpose:
  - no Apple binary (the XNU user space, the iPhone firmware and the IPSW are yours: ios17/version.env
    names the build, sysimage/unpack.sh of the common tree unpacks it)
  - no vendor firmware and no vendor UEFI driver (pull-firmware.sh takes them from your own phone)
  - no decryption key and no circumvention: nothing here defeats a protection.

